# TapAuth PAM module configuration example.
# The distribution packages wire pam_tapauth.so into sudo, su and polkit-1
# automatically (originals kept as <file>.tapauth-bak). To add the line to
# another service file manually (e.g. /etc/pam.d/<service>):
#
#   auth    sufficient    pam_tapauth.so
#
# All fingerprint stacks (kde-fingerprint, gdm-fingerprint, fingerprint-auth)
# stay stock: they call pam_fprintd.so, which resolves to tapauthd's virtual
# fprintd D-Bus service (net.reactivated.Fprint). Lock screens and greeters
# therefore work out of the box — no local fingerprint reader required, and
# the real fprintd daemon stays dormant (no package conflict).
#
# To keep a real local fingerprint reader instead, set
# enable_fprintd_bridge = false in /etc/tapauth/config.toml.
